  "checks": [
    {
      "item": "Actual Gaussian representation and width",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "Square factors have the actual covariance, projected laws are actual Gaussian pushforwards, and gP is the actual integral of the projected infinity norm. No rank or inverse-covariance premise."
    },
    {
      "item": "Zero-variance and negative thresholds",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "CoordinateL2 and centering force actual zero-variance linear forms to vanish almost surely; the Gaussian transpose-kernel identity gives the same under its actual law. Nonnegative omitted thresholds preserve both probabilities; negative thresholds make both zero. The original and retained threshold suprema are equal."
    },
    {
      "item": "Empty retained family",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "The positive count may vanish. Both discrepancy and width are then exactly zero, and all rates vanish without applying a positive-dimension CLT. The retained count matches the paper after renaming remaining faces."
    },
    {
      "item": "Bounded fourth-moment substitution",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "Actual projected bounded-independent summands have envelopeJ\u03b4; same-observation and independent-copy quadratic fourth budgets separately transport atJ\u00b2s4. The new intrinsic bounded theorem supplies the rate."
    },
    {
      "item": "Unconditional bounded-envelope branch",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "The public simpler-envelope contract assumes boundedness alone. It constructs both fourth budgets internally at\u03b4\u00b2; no supplied relative-fourth premise remains."
    },
    {
      "item": "Envelope-only polynomial class",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "Finite q-envelope moments withq>2 supply coordinateL2 and centering. The actual projected qmoment is bounded at(JB)^q and average second moments are one. No coordinate-fourth assumption is introduced, including2<q<4."
    },
    {
      "item": "Polynomial fourth class and averaging",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "Weighted fourth control is averaged over observations before fixed face coefficients are summed. It givesJ\u2074B\u00b2=(J\u00b2B)\u00b2. SinceJ\u22651, J\u00b2B is a safe common scale for the envelope and coordinate-fourth budgets."
    },
    {
      "item": "Minimum and universal constants",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "One positive Cq is obtained from newTheorem2 before dimensions, probability models, arrays,B,normals andJ. With fourth moments, the envelope rate atJB and fourth rate atJ\u00b2B are minimized with that sameCq. The bounded/Orlicz coefficient likewise precedes every model."
    },
    {
      "item": "Orlicz branch integration",
      "status": "passed_with_author_disclosure",
      "details": "The two self-authored files supply exactJK projection inputs and the actual gP-dependent Cor2 endpoint. The independently reviewed assembly introduces no extra comparison/normalization premise. Independent source coverage of these two needs another reviewer."
    },
    {
      "item": "Width and dimension",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "All rates recompute dimensionLog and auxiliary functions at the positive retained count. A purely Gaussian construction givesgP\u22642sqrt(log(e*k)) without any observation-array assumption; k\u2264m yields the printed worst-case order."
    },
    {
      "item": "Raw boundedness and moment finiteness semantics",
      "status": "passed",
      "details": "The bounded contract includes actual a.e. infinity-norm bounds on each independent vector summand and a nonnegative\u03b4. Polynomial qmoments are genuinely Integrable, as well as bounded by actual integral budgets; no finite-second/fourth condition is inferred merely from a totalized numerical integral inequality. Envelope-only projections derive second integrability fromq>2 and never assume raw boundedness of the unbounded observations."
    }
